## ðŸ”¹ GitHub Actions & CI/CD Basics

### Workflow Structure

A GitHub Actions workflow YAML file generally looks like this:

``` yaml
name: CI Pipeline

on:
  push:       # Triggers on every push
  workflow_dispatch:   # Allows manual trigger

jobs:
  build:               # Job name (can be anything)
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - name: Checkout code
        uses: actions/checkout@v3
```

### Trigger Options (`on:`)

-   `push` â†’ Run on every push\
-   `pull_request` â†’ Run on pull request events\
-   `workflow_dispatch` â†’ Run manually\
-   `schedule` â†’ Run on cron schedule\
-   `release` â†’ Run on release events

### Important Jobs

-   `runs-on` â†’ Defines OS (ubuntu-latest, windows-latest,
    macos-latest)\
-   `steps` â†’ Defines each action/command\
-   `uses` â†’ Use a predefined GitHub Action\
-   `run` â†’ Run a shell command

